{"id":91,"date":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/six-things-to-know-before-switching-your-allentown-home-to-a-heat-pump\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:53","slug":"six-things-to-know-before-switching-your-allentown-home-to-a-heat-pump","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/six-things-to-know-before-switching-your-allentown-home-to-a-heat-pump\/","title":{"rendered":"Heat Pumps Work in Allentown\u2014but Does Your House?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignfull has-media-on-the-right s-hero-split wp-elements-bcae8681e5c7cc6dade941f85896b012\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading s-hero-split__text wp-block-heading\">Heat pumps work. Your house might not.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The heat pump question in the Lehigh Valley isn&#039;t whether the technology works in winter anymore. It&#039;s whether your house \u2014 its ducts, its panel, its backup plan \u2014 is ready to let it.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book Winter Readiness<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser.png\" alt=\"condenser - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1794\" style=\"object-fit:cover;height:100%\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez3-condenser-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The spec line that matters<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every heat pump has a rated capacity, and most marketing quotes it at 47 degrees \u2014 weather that barely counts as winter here. The line that predicts your January is capacity at 5\u00b0F. True cold-climate units hold 80 to 100 percent of rated output at that mark; bargain units fall off a cliff below freezing and lean on expensive electric-resistance backup for the season&#039;s whole second act.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Lehigh Valley&#039;s design temperature sits in the single digits, and valley inversions hold cold snaps for days. Spec for that reality: we put the 5\u00b0F number, from the manufacturer&#039;s expanded performance tables, in writing on every heat-pump proposal. Ask anyone quoting you to do the same.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Sized to measured load, not builder assumptions<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Capacity verified at 5\u00b0F outdoor design temperature<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Dual-fuel switchover calculated from your PPL rates<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Defrost cycles scheduled for off-peak hours where available<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1.png\" alt=\"minisplit - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1765\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-minisplit-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b.jpg\" alt=\"attic insulation\" class=\"wp-image-189\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;The R11 attic insulation&quot; by zieak, BY, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Your ductwork has opinions<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Furnaces deliver scorching air through ducts sized for it; heat pumps deliver larger volumes of warm-not-hot air, and duct systems built for the old regime can choke the new one. The symptom is a unit that runs constantly while the far rooms never quite arrive \u2014 and the fix belongs in the proposal, not in the callback. Before we size equipment, we measure static pressure and inspect the return paths.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Allentown&#039;s mid-century housing typically needs return upgrades \u2014 bigger grilles, an added return run, jump ducts to bedrooms \u2014 and sometimes a trunk modification. It&#039;s unglamorous money, but it&#039;s the difference between a heat pump that delights and one that disappoints.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Static pressure test identifies chokepoints<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Return-air sizing matches heat pump CFM demand<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Jump ducts and grille upgrades budgeted upfront<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Insulation and sealing reduce duct leakage loss<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">West End rowhomes versus township colonials<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The conversion looks different across the city. West End rowhomes with radiator heat often skip ducts entirely \u2014 multi-zone ductless with heads per floor, boiler retained or retired case by case. The postwar ranches and township colonials usually have workable ducts that need return-side surgery. And the new construction east of the city mostly needs nothing but correctly sized equipment.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Allentown&#039;s older neighborhoods near Hamilton and Seventh present the densest concentration of heat-pump conversion candidates in the Valley: homes built for coal or oil heat, electrical services upgraded decades ago to marginal adequacy, and insulation that reflects whatever decade the last owner tackled the attic. These houses benefit enormously from heat-pump efficiency but require the most careful system design.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Backup heat is a design decision<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Below some outdoor temperature, every heat pump needs help. What form that help takes should be chosen on purpose. Electric strip heat is cheap to install and brutal to run \u2014 fine as a rarely-used floor, bad as a plan. Keeping your existing gas furnace as the backup \u2014 dual fuel \u2014 lets the system switch fuels automatically at the outdoor temperature where gas becomes the cheaper BTU, which our controls set from your actual utility rates.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-icon-list\">\n<li>Dual-fuel mode arbitrages natural gas and electricity in real time<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Electric-only path requires oversized cold-climate equipment and panel upgrade<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Lockout logic prevents short-cycling and controls auxiliary heat cost<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Switchover temperature modeled against twelve months of your actual bills<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Outage resilience planned before startup \u2014 no surprises in January<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--ember\">\n<li>PPL time-of-use rates save 20% with off-peak defrost scheduling<\/li>\n\n\n<li>IRA + PA Act 129 rebates stack to $8,000 on cold-climate units<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Cold-climate capacity holds at 5\u00b0F \u2014 matches Lehigh Valley design winter<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Panel upgrade costs $2,000\u20133,500 but unlocks full electrification<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Load calculation precedes equipment selection \u2014 always<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Money: what the rebates actually cover<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Current incentives materially change the math, and they stack. The paperwork is part of our scope \u2014 you shouldn&#039;t need a tax attorney to buy a heat pump. As of this writing, an Allentown conversion can draw on the federal 25C tax credit \u2014 thirty percent of installed cost up to its annual cap for qualifying cold-climate equipment \u2014 plus PPL&#039;s residential rebates for high-efficiency heat pumps, filed per unit.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Whole-home electrification incentives apply where income-qualified and can be substantial. Off-peak and time-of-use rate plans reward the heat pump&#039;s steady draw and are worth enrolling in at switchover. Manufacturer promotions surface seasonally; we track them so quotes reflect the current stack, not last spring&#039;s offer.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Federal 25C tax credit: 30% of installed cost, annual cap<\/li>\n\n\n<li>PPL residential rebates: per unit, stacked with federal incentive<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Whole-home electrification: income-qualified, substantial where eligible<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Time-of-use enrollment: discount defrost cycles to off-peak hours<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Manufacturer seasonal promotions: tracked and applied at quote time<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1.png\" alt=\"thermostat - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1761\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Is your house ready for a heat pump?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Electrical panel has 40+ amps of unused breaker space \u2014 sufficient for heat pump circuit<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Existing ductwork reaches all rooms without major leaks \u2014 airflow adequate for heat pump<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Attic and walls insulated to R-30\/R-13 minimum \u2014 envelope tight enough for heat pump efficiency<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Current heating costs above $2,500\/year \u2014 savings justify the investment timeline<\/li>\n\n\n<li>No gas appliances besides furnace \u2014 full electrification feasible in one project<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Heat-pump questions from the Valley<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Will it really keep up in a cold snap?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sized to the load and specced at 5\u00b0F, yes \u2014 through precisely the weather that built the old reputation. The failures people cite are almost always sizing or duct failures wearing the technology&#039;s name.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What happens to my bill?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Versus oil, propane, or electric resistance: down, usually dramatically. Versus cheap natural gas: roughly a wash on heating with dual fuel doing the arbitrage, plus a more efficient summer. We model it from twelve months of your actual bills before you commit.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How loud is the outdoor unit?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Modern variable-speed condensers run in the fifties of decibels at low speed \u2014 conversation volume \u2014 and they idle along at low speed most of the time. Placement still matters near bedroom windows and property lines, so it&#039;s part of the site plan.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>My electrical panel is full \u2014 does that kill the conversion?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Not necessarily. Many panels can support a heat pump through load management: moving circuits, combining runs, or installing a load-sharing controller that sequences high-draw equipment. A panel inspection tells us whether you have spare capacity hiding behind a full breaker directory, or whether an upgrade belongs in the scope.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-nearby has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Also serving nearby:<\/strong> <a href=\"\/historic-districts-fresh-air-ventilation-done-right-in-bethlehem\/\">Bethlehem<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"\/is-it-time-to-replace-that-aging-air-conditioner-in-your-easton-home\/\">Easton<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"\/oil-tank-on-its-last-legs-conversion-options-for-quakertown-homes\/\">Quakertown<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" data-id=\"1756\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-t